## The order
  1 BASS MUSIC, deepest first — wubs, dubs, drops: anything dubstep, EDM or bass. Tools reach full depth (eravos.tool-depth.spec,
    D1 Wobble Bass → D2 Reese → D3 the Wub components → the drop and sub tools), and their sound packs (eravos.genre-packs.spec).
  2 SYNTHWAVE in full — its tools (the P74b.4 gaps: gated reverb, FM keys, brass stabs, ensemble chorus, vocoder) and its pack.
  3 OUTWARD — full music: VOICE (eravos.phase75-map V: Autotune and the vocal chain), GUITAR, DRUMS (acoustic and electronic kits),
    keys and ensemble (phase75-map G1–G4), then the genre families that use them (G5).

## Packs feel like DLC ("dlc would be cool though")
  A pack is a full pack of SOUNDS for every tool it fits (genre-packs.spec, third addendum), presented and handled like DLC: a Packs
  page with a card per pack (art, what it adds in numbers, a demo to hear first), Install / Uninstall, and nothing left behind when
  uninstalled. A pack never ships tools; tool power comes from tool depth.

## Pattern Library: categories beyond EDM ("this isn't only for edm")
  Two axes, both visible on the page:
    WHAT IT IS   role categories that cover full music: Drums · Percussion · Bass · Chords & Keys · Lead & Melody · Arp · Guitar ·
                 Voice (melodies and rhythms to sing or rap, Lyric Rhythm flows) · Strings & Ensemble · FX & Risers · Drops ·
                 Fills · Curves · Tension · Build → Drop. A role with no patterns yet shows as "coming" (honest, not hidden).
    WHERE IT'S FROM  top-level families: Bass music (dubstep, riddim, DnB, …) · EDM & dance (house, techno, trance, …) · Synth & retro
                 (synthwave, darkwave, …) · Hip-hop & R&B · Pop · Rock & guitar · Jazz & soul · World · Chill & ambient · Cinematic ·
                 Collections — the 3.73 families regrouped under these, ready for the genres phase75-map G5 adds.
  Every pattern carries role + family + genre; new genres and instruments add patterns into these without changing the page.

